---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Privacy and Local Data | teleprompter.wtf';
const description =
  'Studio keeps scripts, ideas, settings and recordings in your browser on this device. Learn how local storage and self-hosted Umami analytics work.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="prose-page section-wrap">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">Privacy</span>
    </nav>
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h1>Your work stays on your device.</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose-body">
      <h2>Studio storage</h2><p>
        Studio stores scripts, ideas, settings, reminders, streak dates and take chunks in IndexedDB
        on this device. The classic editor uses browser-local storage. A transfer code contains
        scripts and settings when you choose to copy it; it never contains takes.
      </p>
      <h2>Recordings and exports</h2><p>
        The camera and microphone stream is recorded in your browser. Takes remain in browser
        storage until you share or download them. Nothing is uploaded by the app. Browser storage
        can be cleared by the browser or by you, so save important takes to Photos or Files
        promptly. Private browsing may lose takes when the tab closes.
      </p>
      <h2>Offline use and reminders</h2><p>
        The Home Screen app caches pages and assets for offline use. Calendar reminders are
        generated as a file on your device; there is no reminder server. You can remove a reminder
        in your calendar.
      </p>
      <h2>Usage measurement</h2><p>
        We use self-hosted Umami to measure page views and product actions with a random device
        identifier stored in your browser. Events never contain script text, titles, idea text, file
        names or recording content.
      </p>
      <h2>Remove data</h2><p>
        Delete scripts and takes in Studio, or remove all site data in your browser settings. To ask
        a question, use the <a href="https://github.com/SABYA648/Telemprompter-WTF/issues"
          >project issue tracker</a
        > without private content.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
